/P 113 0 R
/E (When we write NumPy code in Python, the heavy computation actually happens in C. NumPy stores data in one continuous block of memory. This idea of keeping data close together in memory is called spatial locality. Because NumPy arrays use spatial locality, they are much faster than Python lists.)
